argon-utils (0.1.13) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Ship /usr/share/argon-utils/overlays/argon-oneup-lid.dtbo: a
    device-tree overlay that makes the Argon ONE UP's lid (GPIO27) a
    standard SW_LID switch, so logind handles it like any laptop lid.
    Not enabled by the package; see the packaging README.
  * Build-Depends: device-tree-compiler.

 -- Simon Keimer <dc0sk@mailbox.org>  Sat, 19 Sep 2026 09:30:00 +0200

argon-utils (0.1.12) unstable; urgency=medium

  * postinst asks the bus daemon to reload its policy once the argon user
    exists. On a first install the daemon had already reloaded when the
    policy file was unpacked -- before the user existed -- and dropped the
    rule naming it, so argond was refused its bus name until the next
    reload. Seen on a fresh install on the ONE UP.
  * Desktop notifications say "Battery", like the tray, instead of "UPS".

 -- Simon Keimer <dc0sk@mailbox.org>  Sat, 19 Sep 2026 02:00:00 +0200

argon-utils (0.1.11) unstable; urgency=medium

  * The tray says "Battery" instead of "UPS" (e.g. "Battery 92 % · on
    mains", "Battery 9 % · critical"), and the OLED "BAT" (e.g. "BAT 92%"):
    on a ONE UP the battery is the laptop's own, not a UPS.

 -- Simon Keimer <dc0sk@mailbox.org>  Sat, 19 Sep 2026 01:30:00 +0200

argon-utils (0.1.10) unstable; urgency=medium

  * argond.service no longer lists argononeupd.service under Conflicts=.
    Starting argond stopped the ONE UP's vendor daemon, which also holds
    the lid switch, with nothing recorded to restore it. argond already
    stays in dry run while that daemon runs; reading the fuel gauge
    alongside it is safe. A test now keeps Conflicts= equal to the UPS
    vendor units the package retires and restores.

 -- Simon Keimer <dc0sk@mailbox.org>  Sat, 19 Sep 2026 01:00:00 +0200

argon-utils (0.1.9) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Argon ONE UP battery: with [ups] source = "oneup", argond reads the
    laptop's Cellwise CW2217 fuel gauge (reads only, identified by its
    VERSION register first) into the same battery policy, delayed
    poweroff and status file as the PWR UPS. It acts only in mode "full"
    and only while the vendor's argononeupd is not running.
  * argonctl battery: read the ONE UP's gauge by hand.
  * On the ONE UP, CanPoweroffWithWake answers "na", so the tray does not
    offer a wake the hardware cannot do.

 -- Simon Keimer <dc0sk@mailbox.org>  Fri, 18 Sep 2026 22:00:00 +0200

argon-utils (0.1.8) unstable; urgency=medium

  * The tray shows any shutdown logind has scheduled -- including one it
    asked argond for, with the time the UPS will wake the machine -- and
    offers to cancel it. It no longer offers "Power off now…" on top of a
    shutdown that is already scheduled.

